--------------------------------------------------------------------------
On the one alarming-looking line
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Failed to get logical address" at 120.674 is the interface function's FIRST
probe attempt, which ran before the control function had powered the codec.
Its address query legitimately failed and the probe returned -EPROBE_DEFER.
The control function then brought the part up at 120.729, and the deferred
probe was retried at 120.740 and succeeded with laddr 0xca.

This is correct behaviour, and it confirms the dependency is real rather than
theoretical: the interface function genuinely cannot enumerate until the
control function has powered the codec. The ordering resolves itself through
the normal driver model, with no explicit sequencing in the driver.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Milestone
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Lumia 1520's WCD9320 exposes both PGD and IFD SLIMbus functions. Both
enumerate with independent logical addresses; the PGD exclusively owns codec
power and reset and identifies Taiko silicon, while the IFD binds without any
regulator or reset activity.
